{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29173 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Platyphyllone is implicated in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through a multi-step pathway involving CAKI-2 and other compounds. The evidence suggests that Platyphyllone acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 3-Methylhexan-1-ol and (1S,9S,10R,12R,13S,14S)-5,5,9,13-tetramethylpentacyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,9.012,14]hexadecan-6-one, which in turn target Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates that Platyphyllone may exert its effects through these intermediates, potentially modulating the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C in a complex regulatory network. The presence of multiple targets and the involvement of different compounds suggest a possible role in signaling pathways that influence cellular function, though the exact mechanism of interaction between Platyphyllone and Phosphodiesterase 6C remains to be fully elucidated.",
